RUN. SLICE. REPEAT. &#x1F355;&#x1F3C3;&#x2640;&#xFE0F;

En agosto con <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/sbarro?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Sbarro</a>, realizamos una colaboraci&#xF3;n juanto a <a class="link" href="https://de.linkedin.com/company/adidas?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>adidas</a> en el marco de la Media Marat&#xF3;n de Buenos Aires, uno de los eventos deportivos m&#xE1;s importantes del a&#xF1;o, llevando The Original NY Pizza XXL a la comunidad de adidas Runners.

Fui parte de la acci&#xF3;n desde un lugar que disfruto mucho: la creaci&#xF3;n y cobertura de contenido en tiempo real, buscando capturar esos momentos que hacen a la experiencia: la alegr&#xED;a de cada runner al cruzar la meta y luego, por supuesto, disfrutar una slice de Sbarro.
Tambi&#xE9;n trabajamos en el desarrollo de una c&#xE1;psula especial de comunicaci&#xF3;n, junto a Lucia Cosimanoy <a class="link" href="https://ar.linkedin.com/in/romina-ormazabal?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Romina Ormazabal</a>.

Una colaboraci&#xF3;n que nos permiti&#xF3; descubrir un punto de conexi&#xF3;n entre dos marcas con mundos diferentes y construir una experiencia relevante para sus comunidades.

Menci&#xF3;n especial al equipo de <a class="link" href="https://ar.linkedin.com/company/5yardas?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Cinco Yardas</a> por acompa&#xF1;arnos en esta acci&#xF3;n. &#x1F91D;

Today on <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fnationalfarmersday&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#NationalFarmersDay</a>, we celebrate the growers and farm families who keep our communities moving forward. &#x1F69C;&#x1F4E6;

At Pratt Industries, supporting local agriculture is at the core of what we do. Our expanded Moultrie warehouse is just one of the ways we are increasing capacity, service, and sustainable packaging solutions for Georgia&#x2019;s farming community.

Thank you to our agricultural partners today and every day! Learn more about our Moultrie expansion on the blog: <a class="link" href="https://bit.ly/46zT7xr?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://bit.ly/46zT7xr</a>

Happy National Pizza Month! &#x1F355;

Behind every great slice is a box built to protect it. At Pratt Industries, we manufacture custom, 100% recycled, and recyclable pizza boxes designed to keep your pizza hot, fresh, and sustainably packaged.

Learn more about our sustainable pizza packaging: <a class="link" href="https://bit.ly/4mUUxrI?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://bit.ly/4mUUxrI</a>

As a privately owned and locally operated packaging leader, Pratt Agriculture brings the speed and flexibility your farm needs.

Because our decisions are made locally, we can quickly stock our warehouses with tailored agricultural packaging solutions designed specifically for your produce operations. From field to market, we help ensure your crops get the protection they deserve, when you need it. &#x1F4E6;

Discover how our local team can support your packaging needs: <a class="link" href="https://bit.ly/44A985K?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://bit.ly/44A985K</a>

Growth is important but responsible growth matters even more. 

In franchise development, knowing when to say &#x201C;no&#x201D; can be just as important as knowing when to say &#x201C;yes.&#x201D; 

In an article from Pizza Marketplace, Marco&#x2019;s Pizza Chief Development Officer Gerardo Flores shares why disciplined growth is at the heart of our development strategy. From evaluating market capacity and real estate analytics to franchisee readiness and cultural fit, every decision is made with the long-term health of the brand and our franchisees in mind. 

At Marco&#x2019;s, we believe successful franchising isn&#x2019;t simply about signing more deals or opening more locations. It&#x2019;s about building the right markets, with the right partners, in the right locations and creating opportunities for long-term success. 

As Gerardo puts it, &#x201C;Discipline, not velocity, is the real differentiator for a development strategy built to last.&#x201D; 

Read the full article in Pizza Marketplace: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gU24pijh?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gU24pijh</a>

Congratulations to franchisee Fulton Juez on your recent Marco&apos;s store opening in North Miami Beach, FL. 

A new Marco&#x2019;s store opened up at 3115 NE 163rd St. in North Miami Beach, FL. If you are in the area, be sure to stop in and place an order to support this new store!&#xA0; 

Congratulations Fulton, your team, and your area representative on this exciting milestone. Wishing you continued success as you serve your new communities!&#xA0;

