Yesterday, we hosted <a class="link" href="https://ca.linkedin.com/company/women-in-tech-sales-wits?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Women in Tech Sales (WITS)</a> in our Toronto office for an honest conversation about what separates top sellers from everyone else.

40 women showed up to hear from <a class="link" href="https://ca.linkedin.com/in/katarina-r-65902595?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Katarina R.</a>, <a class="link" href="https://ca.linkedin.com/in/kathrine-orlowski-b81830112?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Kathrine Orlowski</a>, and Shikha Bindra.

A few things that stood out:

&#x2192; Politeness isn&apos;t pipeline. A prospect who loved the demo isn&apos;t necessarily a qualified deal. Did the conversation create enough value for them to actually act?

&#x2192; Top sellers aren&apos;t necessarily working the hardest. They&apos;re intentional about where they spend their time and which accounts deserve their attention.

&#x2192; AI is becoming a seller&apos;s job, too. The question isn&apos;t whether your company is building workflows for you. The sellers getting ahead are figuring out how to build and use them themselves. &#x1F916; 

From there, we broke into mentoring circles - smaller groups, experienced mentors, and candid conversations about what&apos;s actually hard right now. &#x1F4AC; 

The event sold out weeks in advance, with the waitlist moving right up until the event. A pretty great reminder of what happens when women create space to learn from and support each other. We&apos;re proud to continue our partnership with WITS as a Silver Hiring Partner and connect with the next cohort of women building careers in tech sales. &#x1F91D; 

&#x1F680;  What&apos;s next? The WITS Bootcamp is coming up next week, bringing together women looking to break into B2B SaaS sales, build their networks, and connect with tech employers.

