48 hours ago, we launched the <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/olo?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Olo</a> App. Since then, I&#x2019;ve read every comment, article, and DM. I&#x2019;ve answered as many questions as I can. Here are the four I see most:

&#x201C;Isn&#x2019;t this just another third-party marketplace?&#x201D;
No. It&#x2019;s a network, not a marketplace, for good reason. Every order hits the restaurant&#x2019;s kitchen exactly like a first-party order with zero commission. The brand keeps the guest relationship and the data. The Olo App brings restaurants together as a coalition.

&#x201C;Will people really download another app?&#x201D;
40 million guests already have an Olo Account. Sign in with your email or mobile number, and your favorite brands, order history, delivery addresses, and payment details come with you. We built this for the big middle: guests who love variety and don&#x2019;t want to pay 15-30% more for it.

&#x201C;Isn&#x2019;t the 5% fee just a commission by another name?&#x201D;
No. The guest pays 5% on top of the product subtotal. The restaurant pays zero commission and keeps the full profit of a first-party order. We show the fee at the top of the menu and again at checkout. Want the absolute lowest price? Order direct from the brand&#x2014;we tell you that in the fee breakdown at checkout.

&#x201C;Who delivers?&#x201D;
More than two dozen delivery service providers through Olo Dispatch. We built delivery-as-a-service over a decade ago and have scaled it ever since. Those years also gave us answers to the hard questions on driver accountability, handoffs, and reconciliation.

The Olo App is not an all-encompassing solution today. Circle back with us in 2030. We have big plans we&#x2019;re already working toward. 

Until then: feedback and iteration. 
Miles to go before we sleep! &#x1F680;

